ALEPH-NULL  (ℵ₀)  —  STRUCTURE
============================================================
511.3 Set theory (cardinals, ordinals, ℵ₀, continuum c, etc.)
Definition:
  ℵ₀ = the cardinality class of all sets admitting a bijection
        with the natural numbers N = {0,1,2,3,...}.

Structural Interpretation:
  ℵ₀ = |ω|
    where:
      ω = the first infinite ordinal
      |·| = the cardinal-collapse map (forgetting order)

  Thus:
      ω + ω = ω·2 ≠ ω   ordinal ω  → encodes order-type
      |ω + ω| = ℵ₀      cardinal ℵ₀ → encodes size-type

Countable Sets:
  A set X is countable  ⇔  ∃ bijection f : X → N.
  Examples:
    - N (naturals)
    - Z (integers)
    - Q (rationals)
  All have cardinality ℵ₀.

Uncountable Sets:
  Some sets cannot be indexed by N.
  Example:
    - R (reals) has cardinality c > ℵ₀.

Algebra of ℵ₀:
  Finite additions:
      ℵ₀ + n = ℵ₀
      ℵ₀ · n = ℵ₀

  Countable additions/products:
      ℵ₀ + ℵ₀ = ℵ₀
      ℵ₀ · ℵ₀ = ℵ₀

  Structural reason:
      ω ⊔ ω   has order-type ω
      ω × ω   has a bijection with ω (diagonal enumeration)

Why ℵ₀ is “smallest infinite”:
  - No finite cardinal equals ℵ₀.
  - Any infinite cardinal κ satisfies κ ≥ ℵ₀.
  - ℵ₀ is the initial infinite fixed point of bijection-size.

Summary:
  ℵ₀ is the base unit of infinite cardinality:
      the size of any set indexable by ω,
      stable under finite and countable algebraic operations,
      and strictly smaller than the continuum c.

OPERATOR FORM OF ALEPH-NULL (ℵ₀)
------------------------------------------------------------

Object:
  ℵ₀  :=  | ω |

Interpretation:
  |·|  =  Cardinal-Collapse Operator
  ω    =  Minimal Infinite Ordinal (RDG-ordinal mode)

Thus:
  ℵ₀ is the SIZE-INVARIANT of ω under collapse.

Tri-Mode Embedding
------------------------------------------------------------

SID (Structure–Interaction–Dynamics):

  S-mode (Structure):
      S(ℵ₀) := EquivClass( X , X ≅ N )
      where N = {0,1,2,...}

  I-mode (Interaction):
      I(ℵ₀) :=  Bij( X , N )
      (existence of a bijection defines membership in ℵ₀-class)

  D-mode (Dynamics):
      D(ℵ₀) := Closure under:
                 - finite sum
                 - finite product
                 - countable sum
                 - countable product
               encoded as:
                 ℵ₀ ⊕ ℵ₀ = ℵ₀
                 ℵ₀ ⊗ ℵ₀ = ℵ₀

Operator-Clean Notation
------------------------------------------------------------

  ℵ₀  =  Card( ω )
       =  Collapse_Ω( ω )
       =  Ω₀

Where:
  Card(·)        = cardinal abstraction operator
  Collapse_Ω(·)  = RDG collapse-to-cardinality operator
  Ω₀             = RDG name for the initial infinite cardinal

